  "ownership_review": [
    "s.object uses beforeAllocation, JS_NewObject and checkedAllocation, then owns the new object within operation Scope.",
    "a.duplicate gives the bootstrap result a distinct reference. a.expression calls Scope.finish and Boundary.finish, which releases tracked Scope values and returns the escaped result only on success; failureRoots releases the result on any completion failure.",
    "init registers local defer immediately after the successful expression. Any later setup failure releases that local before the existing earlier errdefer destroys Fixture/Engine.",
    "callbacks.Scope.init duplicates the resource into its stable self.resource before pushing its address into Environment.native_resources; the Environment vector borrows that stable address.",
    "After successful init, the local defer retires its reference while CallbackScope retains its own. Scope.deinit closes/pops and releases self.resource before Environment release.",
    "If Scope.init fails after initialized becomes true, the existing catch marks failed and deinitializes the scope before the local defer and Fixture errdefer run.",
    "The fresh plain object gains no properties pointing to BindingData or FileHandle; collectHandle and dropBindingTarget retain their original ability to remove the tested strong references.",
    "No production source, test body, expected result, observer phase, import, embed or named declaration is changed."
